{
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "kind": "standard",
  "organization": "ScaleDock",
  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Covers the OpenSSF OSV (Open Source Vulnerability) schema at release 1.9.1: every record field (schema_version, id, modified, published, withdrawn, aliases, upstream, related, summary, details, severity with CVSS_V2, CVSS_V3, CVSS_V4 and Ubuntu types and the source attribution, references and credits), affected packages with ecosystem, name, purl and the wildcard name, SEMVER, ECOSYSTEM and GIT ranges with introduced, fixed, last_affected and limit events, the IsVulnerable evaluation algorithm, the defined ecosystems and their suffixes, the database id prefixes, JSON Schema validation, and publishing to and consuming from OSV.dev (API and data dumps). Version lines: 1.9 is current, 1.7 to 1.8, 1.2 to 1.6 and 1.0 are legacy with upgrade checklists, and the unreleased main branch is tracked as a preview. SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out versions, fields, affected and ranges, ecosystems and ids, and publishing and consuming.",
